1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
What's today's video about? It's a conversation at an izakaya (Japanese pub).

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Izakaya Reservations and Seating / A Guide to Booking and Being Seated

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:13,341
Welcome!

4
00:00:13,364 --> 00:00:15,938
Welcome to our izakaya.

5
00:00:15,961 --> 00:00:18,860
Hello, table for two, please.

6
00:00:18,884 --> 00:00:20,650
Certainly.

7
00:00:20,673 --> 00:00:23,676
Do you have a reservation for today?

8
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:27,033
No, we don’t have a reservation.

9
00:00:27,056 --> 00:00:29,023
Certainly.

10
00:00:29,046 --> 00:00:31,479
No problem at all.

11
00:00:31,502 --> 00:00:33,311
That’s a relief!

12
00:00:33,334 --> 00:00:35,868
Do you smoke?

13
00:00:35,891 --> 00:00:38,741
No, I don’t.

14
00:00:38,764 --> 00:00:41,702
Non-smoking seats, please.

15
00:00:41,725 --> 00:00:43,892
Certainly.

16
00:00:43,915 --> 00:00:47,048
I’ll show you to the non-smoking section.

17
00:00:47,071 --> 00:00:48,688
Thank you.

18
00:00:48,712 --> 00:00:50,802
Is it the table at the back?

19
00:00:50,825 --> 00:00:54,825
Yes, it’s a table in the back.

20
00:00:54,848 --> 00:00:56,692
Right this way, please.

21
00:00:56,716 --> 00:00:59,516
This table is bright and clean!

22
00:00:59,539 --> 00:01:01,436
Thank you.

23
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:04,193
Will this table work for you?

24
00:01:04,216 --> 00:01:07,508
Yes, this is a great spot.

25
00:01:07,532 --> 00:01:10,932
Please place your belongings in this box.

26
00:01:10,955 --> 00:01:12,955
Got it.

27
00:01:12,978 --> 00:01:15,911
Thanks for letting us know.

28
00:01:15,934 --> 00:01:18,272
It’s pretty crowded in here.

29
00:01:18,296 --> 00:01:22,232
It’s Friday, so we have a lot of guests.

30
00:01:22,256 --> 00:01:24,589
I see.

31
00:01:24,612 --> 00:01:27,022
Good thing we got in.

32
00:01:27,046 --> 00:01:29,779
Is the rest of your party coming soon?

33
00:01:29,802 --> 00:01:33,235
Yes, they’ll be here in about five minutes.

34
00:01:33,258 --> 00:01:35,025
Certainly.

35
00:01:35,048 --> 00:01:37,697
I’ll bring the menu right over.

36
00:01:37,721 --> 00:01:39,411
Please do.

37
00:01:39,434 --> 00:01:41,968
Could we also get some water?

38
00:01:41,991 --> 00:01:45,268
Of course, I’ll bring it right away.

39
00:01:45,291 --> 00:01:49,098
What’s this QR code on the table for?

40
00:01:49,122 --> 00:01:53,255
It’s a QR code for ordering with your smartphone.

41
00:01:53,278 --> 00:01:55,122
That’s convenient!

42
00:01:55,145 --> 00:01:58,029
I’ll order from my phone.

43
00:01:58,053 --> 00:02:02,086
We also have paper menus if you’d prefer to use those.

44
00:02:02,109 --> 00:02:04,242
Got it.

45
00:02:04,265 --> 00:02:06,032
Thank you.

46
00:02:06,055 --> 00:02:09,633
Take your time choosing.

47
00:02:09,656 --> 00:02:13,223
Will do, thank you!

48
00:02:13,246 --> 00:02:22,255
You can download today’s video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

49
00:02:22,255 --> 00:02:23,755
Scene 2: The Basics of Customer Service Manners

50
00:02:23,755 --> 00:02:26,633
Good work today, everyone.

51
00:02:26,656 --> 00:02:29,195
Let’s get started with work.

52
00:02:29,219 --> 00:02:31,752
I’m ready—let’s do this!

53
00:02:31,775 --> 00:02:34,433
What should I do first?

54
00:02:34,457 --> 00:02:39,754
First, let’s go over what to do after seating guests.

55
00:02:39,778 --> 00:02:43,258
Got it—I’ll make sure to remember.

56
00:02:43,281 --> 00:02:48,155
Once guests are seated, immediately offer them an oshibori (hot towel).

57
00:02:48,179 --> 00:02:50,589
It's a hot towel.

58
00:02:50,612 --> 00:02:53,020
Should it be warm?

59
00:02:53,043 --> 00:02:57,843
Yes, please give them a warm towel.

60
00:02:57,866 --> 00:02:59,833
Got it.

61
00:02:59,856 --> 00:03:02,500
Should I hand it to them with both hands?

62
00:03:02,523 --> 00:03:08,123
Yes, politely say 'Welcome' as you hand it to them.

63
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:09,780
Got it.

64
00:03:09,803 --> 00:03:12,940
Greet them with a loud, cheerful voice.

65
00:03:12,964 --> 00:03:17,497
Next, place the menu on the table.

66
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:21,120
Should each person get their own menu?

67
00:03:21,144 --> 00:03:26,024
No, two menus per group is enough.

68
00:03:26,048 --> 00:03:28,514
Got it.

69
00:03:28,537 --> 00:03:31,504
Should I serve water as well?

70
00:03:31,528 --> 00:03:36,534
Since this is an izakaya, start by offering cold water or tea.

71
00:03:36,557 --> 00:03:40,757
Should I ask which one they prefer?

72
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:42,747
Good idea.

73
00:03:42,770 --> 00:03:47,451
Ask if they'd like hot tea or cold water.

74
00:03:47,474 --> 00:03:49,927
Got it.

75
00:03:49,950 --> 00:03:53,364
Should I take notes?

76
00:03:53,388 --> 00:03:57,121
Yes, take notes at first. Okay?

77
00:03:57,144 --> 00:04:00,477
I'll prepare a notebook and pen.

78
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:04,734
Then, show them the board with today's specials.

79
00:04:04,757 --> 00:04:08,643
Where is the specials board?

80
00:04:08,666 --> 00:04:12,120
It's on the shelf next to the kitchen.

81
00:04:12,143 --> 00:04:14,156
Got it.

82
00:04:14,179 --> 00:04:16,413
I'll go check.

83
00:04:16,436 --> 00:04:20,678
Once they've decided, have them press the button.

84
00:04:20,701 --> 00:04:24,874
So when the buzzer rings, I should go right away?

85
00:04:24,897 --> 00:04:27,830
Exactly.

86
00:04:27,853 --> 00:04:30,387
Always assist with a smile.

87
00:04:30,410 --> 00:04:32,043
Got it.

88
00:04:32,066 --> 00:04:33,999
I'll do my best!

89
00:04:34,022 --> 00:04:38,075
If you have any questions, feel free to ask.

90
00:04:38,099 --> 00:04:39,766
Got it.

91
00:04:39,790 --> 00:04:42,556
I’m ready—let’s do this!

92
00:04:42,579 --> 00:04:49,684
The link to review today's video is in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

93
00:04:49,684 --> 00:04:51,184
Scene 3: Order Practice / Let's Practice Taking Orders

94
00:04:51,184 --> 00:04:53,584
Welcome!

95
00:04:53,607 --> 00:04:57,293
Are you ready to order?

96
00:04:57,317 --> 00:05:02,590
Yes, we'd like to order drinks first.

97
00:05:02,614 --> 00:05:04,890
Certainly.

98
00:05:04,913 --> 00:05:07,713
What would you like?

99
00:05:07,736 --> 00:05:12,936
For now, two draft beers, please.

100
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:16,233
Two draft beers, got it.

101
00:05:16,256 --> 00:05:18,428
Got it.

102
00:05:18,451 --> 00:05:23,418
Oh, my friend said they'd prefer a highball.

103
00:05:23,441 --> 00:05:30,316
So that's one draft beer and one highball?

104
00:05:30,339 --> 00:05:33,754
Yes, that's perfect.

105
00:05:33,778 --> 00:05:39,044
We can make the highball stronger if you'd like. How does that sound?

106
00:05:39,067 --> 00:05:42,304
Regular strength is fine.

107
00:05:42,328 --> 00:05:44,409
Got it.

108
00:05:44,433 --> 00:05:48,166
Would you like ice in that?

109
00:05:48,189 --> 00:05:52,085
Yes, please add ice.

110
00:05:52,109 --> 00:05:58,509
The draft beer comes in large and small sizes.

111
00:05:58,532 --> 00:06:01,340
Medium size, please.

112
00:06:01,364 --> 00:06:04,097
Medium draft beer, coming right up.

113
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:06,411
Certainly.

114
00:06:06,434 --> 00:06:09,434
Will the drinks come out quickly?

115
00:06:09,457 --> 00:06:14,024
Yes, we'll prepare them right away.

116
00:06:14,047 --> 00:06:15,742
Thank you.

117
00:06:15,765 --> 00:06:18,165
Looking forward to it!

118
00:06:18,188 --> 00:06:21,261
What's today's appetizer?

119
00:06:21,284 --> 00:06:25,217
Today, it's edamame and a small side dish.

120
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,207
Sounds good!

121
00:06:27,230 --> 00:06:29,724
Could we get some appetizers as well, please?

122
00:06:29,748 --> 00:06:32,003
Certainly.

123
00:06:32,026 --> 00:06:35,026
Two orders of appetizers, coming right up.

124
00:06:35,049 --> 00:06:38,882
Is it okay if we order our food later?

125
00:06:38,905 --> 00:06:43,156
Of course! Just let us know when you're ready.

126
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:45,187
Got it.

127
00:06:45,211 --> 00:06:48,277
We'll take our time looking at the menu.

128
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:53,034
Alright, I'll bring you a draft beer and a highball.

129
00:06:53,057 --> 00:06:56,195
Perfect, thank you!

130
00:06:56,218 --> 00:06:58,854
Please wait just a moment.

131
00:06:58,878 --> 00:07:01,912
Sure, we'll be waiting!

132
00:07:01,936 --> 00:07:03,436
Scene 4: Cheers After Work

133
00:07:03,436 --> 00:07:06,120
Good work today!

134
00:07:06,143 --> 00:07:08,745
Our drinks are here!

135
00:07:08,768 --> 00:07:11,228
Good work today!

136
00:07:11,251 --> 00:07:14,136
I'm so thirsty!

137
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:19,693
Well then, cheers to another week of hard work!

138
00:07:19,716 --> 00:07:22,450
Cheers to that!

139
00:07:22,473 --> 00:07:24,839
Let's toast!

140
00:07:24,862 --> 00:07:26,829
Cheers!

141
00:07:26,852 --> 00:07:29,019
Cheers!

142
00:07:29,042 --> 00:07:34,775
Glug, glug... ahhh, that hits the spot!

143
00:07:34,798 --> 00:07:40,246
You're right, this cold beer is amazing!

144
00:07:40,269 --> 00:07:45,157
Beer after work is the best.

145
00:07:45,181 --> 00:07:50,548
This place has such a perfect head on their beer.

146
00:07:50,571 --> 00:07:52,706
It really does!

147
00:07:52,729 --> 00:07:56,104
It's so chilled and easy to drink.

148
00:07:56,127 --> 00:07:59,706
I drank half of it in one gulp!

149
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:03,496
Haha, you're drinking fast!

150
00:08:03,519 --> 00:08:07,418
It was a really busy day today.

151
00:08:07,441 --> 00:08:11,516
We had so much overtime.

152
00:08:11,539 --> 00:08:15,792
That's why this first sip tastes so good.

153
00:08:15,815 --> 00:08:19,382
Let's dig into these edamame appetizers.

154
00:08:19,405 --> 00:08:23,249
Oh, the saltiness is perfect!

155
00:08:23,272 --> 00:08:26,072
It pairs so well with beer.

156
00:08:26,095 --> 00:08:28,982
This is the perfect bar snack.

157
00:08:29,005 --> 00:08:32,239
Don't drink too much, okay?

158
00:08:32,263 --> 00:08:34,339
Don't worry, I'm fine.

159
00:08:34,363 --> 00:08:36,899
Let's just enjoy ourselves tonight.

160
00:08:36,922 --> 00:08:41,701
Yeah, let's order lots of delicious food too!

161
00:08:41,724 --> 00:08:44,005
Sounds good!

162
00:08:44,029 --> 00:08:47,243
Should we look at the menu?

163
00:08:47,267 --> 00:08:50,915
But first, one more sip.

164
00:08:50,938 --> 00:08:53,305
I'll have another sip too.

165
00:08:53,328 --> 00:08:56,102
Mmm, so good.

166
00:08:56,126 --> 00:08:59,261
This is pure bliss.

167
00:08:59,284 --> 00:09:03,096
I'm so glad we came to this izakaya.

168
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:06,920
Let's have a great time chatting tonight.

169
00:09:06,943 --> 00:09:11,283
Absolutely, let's drink together till the end!

170
00:09:11,306 --> 00:09:12,806
Scene 5: How to Decide What to Order

171
00:09:12,806 --> 00:09:17,073
Alright, let's order some food.

172
00:09:17,096 --> 00:09:19,029
Sounds good!

173
00:09:19,052 --> 00:09:21,670
What are you in the mood for?

174
00:09:21,694 --> 00:09:24,927
I'm craving something meaty.

175
00:09:24,950 --> 00:09:29,117
We have karaage and yakitori.

176
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:31,774
Hmm, tough choice.

177
00:09:31,797 --> 00:09:34,332
Which one do you prefer?

178
00:09:34,356 --> 00:09:38,289
I love fried chicken.

179
00:09:38,312 --> 00:09:43,845
Fried chicken is great, but I can’t resist yakitori either.

180
00:09:43,868 --> 00:09:49,302
Do you like salt or sauce on your yakitori?

181
00:09:49,325 --> 00:09:53,858
I love the sweet sauce.

182
00:09:53,881 --> 00:09:57,814
I prefer the light taste of salt.

183
00:09:57,837 --> 00:10:02,304
How about we order an assortment?

184
00:10:02,327 --> 00:10:06,694
An assortment comes with both, right?

185
00:10:06,717 --> 00:10:11,328
You can order both salt and sauce flavors.

186
00:10:11,352 --> 00:10:14,231
That’s a great idea!

187
00:10:14,255 --> 00:10:18,388
Should we add a plate of fried chicken too?

188
00:10:18,411 --> 00:10:20,445
Sounds good!

189
00:10:20,468 --> 00:10:23,305
Let’s get both.

190
00:10:23,328 --> 00:10:25,895
Can we eat all of that?

191
00:10:25,918 --> 00:10:29,851
It might be a lot.

192
00:10:29,874 --> 00:10:33,508
I’m starving, so I’ll be fine.

193
00:10:33,531 --> 00:10:36,864
Let’s order some salad too.

194
00:10:36,887 --> 00:10:39,720
How about Caesar salad?

195
00:10:39,743 --> 00:10:42,230
I love it!

196
00:10:42,254 --> 00:10:44,550
Let’s go with that.

197
00:10:44,573 --> 00:10:47,858
Tofu salad looks delicious too.

198
00:10:47,881 --> 00:10:51,948
How about we stick with Caesar salad today?

199
00:10:51,971 --> 00:10:54,145
Got it.

200
00:10:54,169 --> 00:10:56,602
Sounds good.

201
00:10:56,625 --> 00:10:59,958
An assorted sashimi platter would be nice too.

202
00:10:59,981 --> 00:11:04,434
They have today’s recommended fish.

203
00:11:04,457 --> 00:11:08,824
Should we order both fish and meat?

204
00:11:08,847 --> 00:11:13,023
It might be safer to order a little at a time.

205
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:14,680
Good idea.

206
00:11:14,703 --> 00:11:17,757
Let’s start with meat and salad.

207
00:11:17,781 --> 00:11:19,347
Got it.

208
00:11:19,370 --> 00:11:22,137
Let’s call the waiter.

209
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:23,660
Scene 6: Taking Orders and Recommending Dishes

210
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:26,111
Did you call for me?

211
00:11:26,135 --> 00:11:29,404
May I take your order?

212
00:11:29,427 --> 00:11:33,630
Excuse me, what’s today’s special?

213
00:11:33,654 --> 00:11:38,987
Today’s recommendation is a fresh assorted sashimi platter.

214
00:11:39,010 --> 00:11:42,143
What kind of fish is in it?

215
00:11:42,166 --> 00:11:46,439
It includes tuna, salmon, and amberjack.

216
00:11:46,463 --> 00:11:48,732
That sounds delicious.

217
00:11:48,755 --> 00:11:52,355
Are these the freshest fish right now?

218
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:56,845
They were just delivered from the port this morning.

219
00:11:56,868 --> 00:11:59,901
That’s amazing!

220
00:11:59,924 --> 00:12:02,157
We’ll take one.

221
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:03,780
Thank you.

222
00:12:03,803 --> 00:12:06,437
One assorted sashimi platter, coming right up.

223
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:10,026
Do you have any other popular appetizers?

224
00:12:10,049 --> 00:12:14,666
Our homemade dashimaki tamago is very popular.

225
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:17,166
Dashimaki tamago?

226
00:12:17,190 --> 00:12:19,190
Is it served warm?

227
00:12:19,213 --> 00:12:23,261
Yes, we grill it fresh after you order.

228
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:26,485
It sounds fluffy and delicious.

229
00:12:26,509 --> 00:12:31,349
The dashi flavor makes it truly irresistible.

230
00:12:31,372 --> 00:12:35,612
Then, I'll have one rolled omelet, please.

231
00:12:35,636 --> 00:12:40,636
We also have a mentaiko cheese rolled omelet.

232
00:12:40,659 --> 00:12:44,037
Wait, mentaiko and cheese?

233
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:48,542
It's the most popular choice among our female customers.

234
00:12:48,566 --> 00:12:51,766
Which one would you recommend, the regular or this one?

235
00:12:51,789 --> 00:12:55,875
The mentaiko version pairs perfectly with alcohol.

236
00:12:55,898 --> 00:12:59,501
In that case, I'll go with the mentaiko one.

237
00:12:59,525 --> 00:13:01,558
Certainly.

238
00:13:01,581 --> 00:13:04,581
You're going to love it—it's absolutely delicious.

239
00:13:04,604 --> 00:13:06,891
I can't wait!

240
00:13:06,915 --> 00:13:09,558
Would you like any fried dishes as well?

241
00:13:09,581 --> 00:13:13,948
What's your top recommendation for fried dishes?

242
00:13:13,971 --> 00:13:18,021
I'd recommend Toriten, a specialty from Oita.

243
00:13:18,044 --> 00:13:19,928
Toriten?

244
00:13:19,951 --> 00:13:22,728
It's a dish you eat with ponzu sauce.

245
00:13:22,752 --> 00:13:27,118
It's so light and refreshing—you can eat it endlessly.

246
00:13:27,141 --> 00:13:29,427
I'll take one of those too, please.

247
00:13:29,451 --> 00:13:31,522
Certainly.

248
00:13:31,546 --> 00:13:34,712
That’s a perfect order!

249
00:13:34,735 --> 00:13:36,235
Scene 7: Ordering and Allergy Accommodation

250
00:13:36,235 --> 00:13:39,505
May I take your order?

251
00:13:39,529 --> 00:13:42,746
I'd like to order this fried rice.

252
00:13:42,769 --> 00:13:45,036
That’s the five-ingredient fried rice, correct?

253
00:13:45,059 --> 00:13:46,659
Thank you.

254
00:13:46,682 --> 00:13:52,515
Um, quick question—does it contain shrimp?

255
00:13:52,538 --> 00:13:54,016
Got it.

256
00:13:54,039 --> 00:13:57,016
Yes, shrimp is one of the ingredients.

257
00:13:57,040 --> 00:14:01,573
I have an allergy, so I can't eat shrimp.

258
00:14:01,596 --> 00:14:04,074
I see.

259
00:14:04,098 --> 00:14:06,667
You have an allergy, right?

260
00:14:06,690 --> 00:14:11,023
Would it be possible to make it without shrimp?

261
00:14:11,046 --> 00:14:13,713
Please wait just a moment.

262
00:14:13,736 --> 00:14:16,584
Let me check with the kitchen.

263
00:14:16,608 --> 00:14:19,008
Sorry for the trouble.

264
00:14:19,031 --> 00:14:21,206
I’m ready—let’s do this!

265
00:14:21,230 --> 00:14:23,523
Thank you for waiting.

266
00:14:23,546 --> 00:14:27,152
We can make it without shrimp.

267
00:14:27,176 --> 00:14:29,109
Really?

268
00:14:29,132 --> 00:14:31,099
That’s such a relief!

269
00:14:31,121 --> 00:14:34,855
Are there any other ingredients you're allergic to?

270
00:14:34,878 --> 00:14:38,319
Eggs and pork are fine.

271
00:14:38,342 --> 00:14:40,709
It's just shrimp and crab.

272
00:14:40,732 --> 00:14:42,776
Certainly.

273
00:14:42,799 --> 00:14:45,766
We’ll make it without shrimp.

274
00:14:45,789 --> 00:14:51,189
I’m also not a big fan of green onions—could you reduce them?

275
00:14:51,212 --> 00:14:55,412
We can leave them out entirely if you'd like.

276
00:14:55,435 --> 00:14:59,132
In that case, please leave out the green onions too.

277
00:14:59,155 --> 00:15:01,355
Understood.

278
00:15:01,378 --> 00:15:04,580
No shrimp, no green onions—got it.

279
00:15:04,604 --> 00:15:07,470
Sorry for all the special requests.

280
00:15:07,493 --> 00:15:10,460
Not at all—please don’t worry.

281
00:15:10,483 --> 00:15:14,449
I really appreciate your kind service.

282
00:15:14,472 --> 00:15:18,639
The salad dressing doesn’t contain shrimp, by the way.

283
00:15:18,662 --> 00:15:22,999
Oh, I was actually thinking of ordering a salad too.

284
00:15:23,023 --> 00:15:27,037
It’s a Japanese-style dressing, so you can enjoy it worry-free.

285
00:15:27,061 --> 00:15:31,102
Then, I’ll add a Japanese-style salad as well, please.

286
00:15:31,126 --> 00:15:33,292
Certainly.

287
00:15:33,315 --> 00:15:35,882
So that’s the salad and the fried rice, correct?

288
00:15:35,905 --> 00:15:37,838
I’m ready—let’s do this!

289
00:15:37,861 --> 00:15:41,636
I'll prepare it deliciously for you, so please wait a moment.

290
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:44,936
Sure, I'm looking forward to it!

291
00:15:44,959 --> 00:15:46,459
Scene 8: Differences in Taste Preferences

292
00:15:46,459 --> 00:15:51,426
Everyone has their own food preferences, don't they?

293
00:15:51,449 --> 00:15:53,715
Good idea.

294
00:15:53,738 --> 00:15:57,154
Do you like spicy food?

295
00:15:57,178 --> 00:15:59,850
I love it!

296
00:15:59,873 --> 00:16:04,806
I love mapo tofu and Korean cuisine.

297
00:16:04,829 --> 00:16:06,966
Really?

298
00:16:06,990 --> 00:16:11,556
I can't handle spicy food at all.

299
00:16:11,579 --> 00:16:16,398
What? You can't even eat kimchi?

300
00:16:16,422 --> 00:16:21,467
Kimchi is a bit too spicy for me, unfortunately.

301
00:16:21,491 --> 00:16:23,749
I see.

302
00:16:23,772 --> 00:16:28,439
Do you prefer sweet or mild flavors?

303
00:16:28,462 --> 00:16:34,862
Yes, I love Japanese dishes with rich dashi broth and sweet sauces.

304
00:16:34,885 --> 00:16:36,697
Got it.

305
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:41,287
I’ll have to be careful with today’s order, then.

306
00:16:41,310 --> 00:16:45,743
Do you eat spicy food on your own?

307
00:16:45,766 --> 00:16:50,343
Let’s enjoy some non-spicy dishes together today.

308
00:16:50,367 --> 00:16:52,537
That’s kind of you.

309
00:16:52,561 --> 00:16:54,327
Thank you.

310
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:57,950
Do you like sweet tamagoyaki (Japanese omelet)?

311
00:16:57,974 --> 00:17:00,374
I love it!

312
00:17:00,397 --> 00:17:03,167
It reminds me of my mom’s cooking.

313
00:17:03,191 --> 00:17:05,357
Sounds good!

314
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:09,047
Then let’s order tamagoyaki.

315
00:17:09,070 --> 00:17:13,758
Do you like raw fish like sushi or sashimi?

316
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:16,348
I love it!

317
00:17:16,371 --> 00:17:18,938
I could eat it every day!

318
00:17:18,961 --> 00:17:23,928
I love sashimi too.

319
00:17:23,951 --> 00:17:26,448
We have similar tastes!

320
00:17:26,471 --> 00:17:29,037
That’s great!

321
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:32,394
I love tuna and salmon.

322
00:17:32,417 --> 00:17:36,428
I prefer white fish, though.

323
00:17:36,452 --> 00:17:38,625
Like flounder?

324
00:17:38,648 --> 00:17:41,541
That’s a sophisticated preference.

325
00:17:41,564 --> 00:17:45,043
That would pair well with drinks.

326
00:17:45,067 --> 00:17:50,123
Speaking of drinks, do you like sweet cocktails?

327
00:17:50,147 --> 00:17:53,580
Not really.

328
00:17:53,603 --> 00:17:57,770
I prefer a crispy oolong highball.

329
00:17:57,793 --> 00:18:03,726
I love sweet plum wine and cassis orange.

330
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:08,116
Our tastes are so opposite—it’s interesting!

331
00:18:08,139 --> 00:18:13,141
Differences make conversations more fun.

332
00:18:13,165 --> 00:18:15,131
It really does!

333
00:18:15,154 --> 00:18:19,221
Let’s share our favorite restaurants with each other.

334
00:18:19,244 --> 00:18:21,653
Sounds good!

335
00:18:21,676 --> 00:18:26,692
Next time, I’ll tell you about my favorite Japanese restaurant.

336
00:18:26,716 --> 00:18:32,370
And I’ll share my favorite super-spicy restaurant!

337
00:18:32,393 --> 00:18:36,843
Please go easy on me with that one.

338
00:18:36,867 --> 00:18:38,367
Scene 9: Serving Food and Handling Requests

339
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:41,700
I’ve brought your food.

340
00:18:41,723 --> 00:18:44,456
Here’s your karaage (Japanese fried chicken).

341
00:18:44,479 --> 00:18:48,213
Wow, it looks delicious!

342
00:18:48,236 --> 00:18:51,089
Thank you.

343
00:18:51,112 --> 00:18:54,645
Please enjoy your meal.

344
00:18:54,668 --> 00:18:57,635
Oh, excuse me.

345
00:18:57,658 --> 00:19:00,729
Could I ask you something?

346
00:19:00,752 --> 00:19:03,971
Of course, what is it?

347
00:19:03,995 --> 00:19:08,034
Could you bring us three small plates, please?

348
00:19:08,058 --> 00:19:10,465
Certainly.

349
00:19:10,488 --> 00:19:13,505
Three small plates, please.

350
00:19:13,528 --> 00:19:20,128
Also, I dropped my chopsticks on the floor, so could I get a replacement?

351
00:19:20,151 --> 00:19:22,793
I sincerely apologize for that.

352
00:19:22,817 --> 00:19:26,502
I’ll bring you new chopsticks right away.

353
00:19:26,526 --> 00:19:28,159
Thank you.

354
00:19:28,182 --> 00:19:30,061
That’s such a relief!

355
00:19:30,084 --> 00:19:33,781
Would you like an extra water glass as well?

356
00:19:33,805 --> 00:19:38,405
Oh, could I get two empty glasses, please?

357
00:19:38,428 --> 00:19:42,299
For splitting the bottled beer, right?

358
00:19:42,323 --> 00:19:45,256
Yes, that’s right.

359
00:19:45,279 --> 00:19:47,967
Smaller glasses would be better.

360
00:19:47,990 --> 00:19:50,364
Certainly.

361
00:19:50,388 --> 00:19:53,668
I’ll prepare them immediately.

362
00:19:53,691 --> 00:19:57,191
Could we also get extra towels or hot hand towels?

363
00:19:57,214 --> 00:20:03,393
Of course! I’ll bring you fresh warm hand towels.

364
00:20:03,417 --> 00:20:05,670
Thank you so much for everything.

365
00:20:05,693 --> 00:20:09,761
Not at all—please don’t worry about it!

366
00:20:09,784 --> 00:20:15,879
Everyone here is so kind and efficient!

367
00:20:15,903 --> 00:20:17,480
Thank you.

368
00:20:17,504 --> 00:20:21,937
We’d like to share the food while it’s still hot.

369
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:25,794
I’ll bring everything as quickly as I can!

370
00:20:25,817 --> 00:20:27,217
Please do.

371
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:29,406
Sorry to keep you waiting.

372
00:20:29,429 --> 00:20:33,232
Here are your small plates and chopsticks.

373
00:20:33,255 --> 00:20:35,455
That was fast!

374
00:20:35,478 --> 00:20:37,083
Thank you.

375
00:20:37,107 --> 00:20:41,641
I’ll also place the glasses and hand towels here for you.

376
00:20:41,664 --> 00:20:43,464
Perfect!

377
00:20:43,487 --> 00:20:46,053
Thank you so much, really.

378
00:20:46,076 --> 00:20:50,043
Is there anything else you need?

379
00:20:50,066 --> 00:20:53,320
We’re good for now.

380
00:20:53,344 --> 00:20:55,477
I’ll call you if we need anything else.

381
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:57,000
Scene 10: Handling Orders During a Busy Shift

382
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:02,283
It’s 8 o’clock, and the restaurant is now full.

383
00:21:02,306 --> 00:21:06,139
The order bells are ringing nonstop!

384
00:21:06,162 --> 00:21:08,329
It’s so busy!

385
00:21:08,352 --> 00:21:13,285
Let’s stay calm and handle orders one by one.

386
00:21:13,308 --> 00:21:14,978
Got it.

387
00:21:15,002 --> 00:21:19,294
There are ten drink orders backed up.

388
00:21:19,317 --> 00:21:23,656
I’ll handle the beers and highballs.

389
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:29,113
Then I’ll take care of the sours and soft drinks.

390
00:21:29,136 --> 00:21:31,108
That’s such a relief!

391
00:21:31,132 --> 00:21:34,066
Let’s split up and serve them quickly!

392
00:21:34,089 --> 00:21:39,691
Some tables are waiting for their food.

393
00:21:39,714 --> 00:21:41,650
Which tables?

394
00:21:41,674 --> 00:21:43,956
I'll go check.

395
00:21:43,979 --> 00:21:47,913
Table 5 and Table 8.

396
00:21:47,936 --> 00:21:52,829
I’ll ask the kitchen to hurry.

397
00:21:52,852 --> 00:21:54,386
Please do.

398
00:21:54,408 --> 00:21:58,105
I’ll go apologize to the customers.

399
00:21:58,128 --> 00:22:01,220
That’s very thoughtful of you!

400
00:22:01,243 --> 00:22:03,721
I’m ready—let’s do this!

401
00:22:03,745 --> 00:22:07,155
Phew, I’m starting to sweat.

402
00:22:07,179 --> 00:22:09,857
It’s really hectic, isn’t it?

403
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:14,214
This is the busiest time of the night.

404
00:22:14,237 --> 00:22:15,903
Let’s keep pushing through!

405
00:22:15,927 --> 00:22:17,527
Got it.

406
00:22:17,550 --> 00:22:21,583
I feel so much better working with you, senior.

407
00:22:21,606 --> 00:22:23,940
Likewise!

408
00:22:23,963 --> 00:22:26,849
Your smile is wonderful.

409
00:22:26,872 --> 00:22:31,141
We’ll keep serving customers with a smile.

410
00:22:31,165 --> 00:22:34,698
It’ll quiet down in just one more hour.

411
00:22:34,721 --> 00:22:38,755
Alright, let's buckle down and do our best!

412
00:22:38,778 --> 00:22:42,978
And don’t forget to restock the drinks, please.

413
00:22:43,001 --> 00:22:45,968
Restocking ice and glasses, got it.

414
00:22:45,991 --> 00:22:47,991
Understood.

415
00:22:48,014 --> 00:22:52,581
Please be careful not to get hurt.

416
00:22:52,604 --> 00:22:53,694
Got it.

417
00:22:53,718 --> 00:22:56,596
I’ll watch my step and be careful while moving.

418
00:22:56,619 --> 00:23:00,452
No running—let’s just walk briskly.

419
00:23:00,475 --> 00:23:02,922
Oh, right!

420
00:23:02,946 --> 00:23:05,749
Safety first, after all.

421
00:23:05,773 --> 00:23:10,573
Once the rush is over, let’s enjoy some delicious staff meals!

422
00:23:10,596 --> 00:23:13,596
I’ll work hard looking forward to that!

423
00:23:13,619 --> 00:23:17,352
Alright, the drinks are ready!

424
00:23:17,375 --> 00:23:19,215
Go ahead and take them.

425
00:23:19,238 --> 00:23:20,972
Got it.

426
00:23:20,995 --> 00:23:23,079
I’m on my way!

427
00:23:23,102 --> 00:23:24,602
Scene 11: Handling Delayed Orders

428
00:23:24,602 --> 00:23:27,136
You called for me?

429
00:23:27,159 --> 00:23:29,042
May I help you?

430
00:23:29,065 --> 00:23:30,798
I’m sorry, but...

431
00:23:30,821 --> 00:23:35,291
The food I ordered 30 minutes ago still hasn’t arrived.

432
00:23:35,315 --> 00:23:38,205
I sincerely apologize for the delay.

433
00:23:38,229 --> 00:23:41,029
Which dish was it?

434
00:23:41,052 --> 00:23:45,018
The yakitori platter and yakisoba.

435
00:23:45,041 --> 00:23:49,061
The yakitori platter and yakisoba, correct?

436
00:23:49,085 --> 00:23:51,485
I’ll check on it right away.

437
00:23:51,508 --> 00:23:56,593
The drinks came quickly, but the food is taking forever.

438
00:23:56,616 --> 00:24:00,435
I’m truly sorry for the inconvenience.

439
00:24:00,459 --> 00:24:06,026
Could you check with the kitchen about the current status?

440
00:24:06,049 --> 00:24:09,827
Yes, I’ll go confirm with the kitchen immediately.

441
00:24:09,850 --> 00:24:12,417
Please wait just a moment.

442
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:15,046
Perfect, thank you!

443
00:24:15,070 --> 00:24:17,403
Thank you for waiting.

444
00:24:17,426 --> 00:24:20,517
I’ve checked with the kitchen.

445
00:24:20,540 --> 00:24:22,507
What’s the update?

446
00:24:22,530 --> 00:24:25,497
Was the order received?

447
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:28,855
Yes, the order was placed.

448
00:24:28,878 --> 00:24:31,337
That’s a relief.

449
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:34,493
How much longer will it take?

450
00:24:34,516 --> 00:24:39,250
The yakitori is just finishing up now.

451
00:24:39,273 --> 00:24:42,406
Will it be ready in about 5 minutes?

452
00:24:42,429 --> 00:24:45,796
Yes, I’ll bring it within 3 minutes.

453
00:24:45,818 --> 00:24:48,652
What about the yakisoba?

454
00:24:48,675 --> 00:24:52,716
The yakisoba hasn’t been started yet.

455
00:24:52,740 --> 00:24:56,176
Wait, it hasn’t even started?

456
00:24:56,199 --> 00:24:59,135
That’ll take a while, then.

457
00:24:59,158 --> 00:25:04,246
We’re very busy, so the order got delayed.

458
00:25:04,270 --> 00:25:09,470
I have a last train to catch, so could I cancel the yakisoba?

459
00:25:09,493 --> 00:25:14,826
Yes, since it hasn’t been made yet, cancellation is possible.

460
00:25:14,849 --> 00:25:18,538
Then, I’d like to cancel the yakisoba, please.

461
00:25:18,562 --> 00:25:20,728
Understood.

462
00:25:20,751 --> 00:25:23,446
I sincerely apologize for that.

463
00:25:23,470 --> 00:25:27,637
No, thank *you* for checking on it.

464
00:25:27,660 --> 00:25:32,326
I’ll bring the yakitori right away, so please wait a moment.

465
00:25:32,349 --> 00:25:35,202
Sure, I’ll be waiting—thanks!

466
00:25:35,226 --> 00:25:38,593
I sincerely apologize.

467
00:25:38,616 --> 00:25:40,683
Excuse me.

468
00:25:40,706 --> 00:25:43,106
Sure, I understand.

469
00:25:43,129 --> 00:25:44,629
Scene 12: Venting About Getting Scolded by the Boss

470
00:25:44,629 --> 00:25:48,596
Looks like the drinks are flowing tonight!

471
00:25:48,619 --> 00:25:51,638
Did something happen?

472
00:25:51,661 --> 00:25:57,541
Actually, my boss chewed me out at work today.

473
00:25:57,565 --> 00:26:01,531
What? Seriously?

474
00:26:01,554 --> 00:26:04,521
That sounds rough.

475
00:26:04,544 --> 00:26:09,477
I got yelled at even though it wasn’t my fault.

476
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:12,467
That’s awful.

477
00:26:12,490 --> 00:26:15,523
What happened?

478
00:26:15,546 --> 00:26:22,595
They said the numbers in the document were wrong, but I didn’t even make it.

479
00:26:22,619 --> 00:26:25,266
That’s just unfair!

480
00:26:25,290 --> 00:26:28,544
Did you stand up for yourself?

481
00:26:28,567 --> 00:26:34,034
My boss was so intimidating—I couldn’t say a word.

482
00:26:34,057 --> 00:26:39,623
Ugh, I totally get how frustrating that must feel.

483
00:26:39,646 --> 00:26:43,695
Sorry for bringing up such a downer topic at the izakaya.

484
00:26:43,718 --> 00:26:51,966
No way! This is exactly the place to vent about stuff like that.

485
00:26:51,990 --> 00:26:55,390
Hearing you say that makes me feel better.

486
00:26:55,413 --> 00:26:59,413
Let’s drink away the bad vibes!

487
00:26:59,436 --> 00:27:04,330
Yeah, I feel like drinking my sorrows away tonight.

488
00:27:04,353 --> 00:27:10,330
Workplace relationships are so complicated, aren’t they?

489
00:27:10,354 --> 00:27:12,754
Seriously.

490
00:27:12,777 --> 00:27:15,835
It’s exhausting trying to read the room all the time.

491
00:27:15,859 --> 00:27:22,625
Funny you mention that—I was actually stressing over my junior last week.

492
00:27:22,649 --> 00:27:24,905
Really? What’s going on?

493
00:27:24,928 --> 00:27:27,220
What’s bothering you?

494
00:27:27,244 --> 00:27:32,777
No matter how many times I teach them, they keep making the same mistakes.

495
00:27:32,800 --> 00:27:35,457
That sounds tough.

496
00:27:35,481 --> 00:27:38,374
Teaching is no walk in the park either.

497
00:27:38,398 --> 00:27:43,931
If I’m too nice, it doesn’t work. If I’m strict, they get upset.

498
00:27:43,954 --> 00:27:48,154
Looks like we both have our fair share of work struggles.

499
00:27:48,177 --> 00:27:54,196
That’s why talking it out like this is the best remedy.

500
00:27:54,219 --> 00:27:55,875
It really does!

501
00:27:55,898 --> 00:27:59,065
I already feel so much lighter.

502
00:27:59,088 --> 00:28:02,964
You’re always working so hard—I know that.

503
00:28:02,987 --> 00:28:05,620
I see it.

504
00:28:05,643 --> 00:28:07,377
Thank you.

505
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:09,933
I’m about to cry...

506
00:28:09,956 --> 00:28:14,974
Come on, put on a smile and take a sip of that highball!

507
00:28:14,997 --> 00:28:18,266
Yeah, I’m starting to feel better already.

508
00:28:18,289 --> 00:28:20,746
Let’s toast again!

509
00:28:20,770 --> 00:28:22,807
Sounds good!

510
00:28:22,830 --> 00:28:27,275
Cheers! Let’s tackle tomorrow with everything we’ve got!

511
00:28:27,298 --> 00:28:28,432
Cheers!

512
00:28:28,455 --> 00:28:31,655
Time to reset and power through tomorrow!

513
00:28:31,678 --> 00:28:33,178
Scene 13: The Art of Pouring Beer

514
00:28:33,178 --> 00:28:37,611
Oh, your glass is empty!

515
00:28:37,634 --> 00:28:40,434
Oh, you’re right.

516
00:28:40,457 --> 00:28:42,955
I didn’t even notice.

517
00:28:42,978 --> 00:28:46,469
Shall I pour you a bottle of beer?

518
00:28:46,493 --> 00:28:48,426
Thank you.

519
00:28:48,449 --> 00:28:51,886
Thanks, that’s so kind of you.

520
00:28:51,910 --> 00:28:55,357
Oh, no, no—please, go ahead.

521
00:28:55,380 --> 00:28:58,317
Hold the glass with both hands, please.

522
00:28:58,341 --> 00:29:01,360
Alright, cheers!

523
00:29:01,383 --> 00:29:03,817
Trickle, trickle...

524
00:29:03,840 --> 00:29:07,293
Perfect foam ratio—just right!

525
00:29:07,316 --> 00:29:10,049
Wow, that’s impressive!

526
00:29:10,072 --> 00:29:13,041
The foam is so fluffy!

527
00:29:13,065 --> 00:29:17,799
I practiced pouring like this during a part-time job back in the day.

528
00:29:17,823 --> 00:29:19,589
Got it.

529
00:29:19,612 --> 00:29:22,346
Now that’s pro-level skill!

530
00:29:22,369 --> 00:29:24,056
Thank you.

531
00:29:24,079 --> 00:29:28,365
Your glass is getting low too, isn’t it?

532
00:29:28,389 --> 00:29:31,227
Oh, you’re right!

533
00:29:31,250 --> 00:29:34,823
What should we drink next?

534
00:29:34,846 --> 00:29:38,646
I’d love to try some sake.

535
00:29:38,669 --> 00:29:41,269
Great choice!

536
00:29:41,292 --> 00:29:45,177
Would you prefer chilled sake or warm?

537
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:48,434
I’d like something crisp—chilled sake, please.

538
00:29:48,457 --> 00:29:53,590
Then let’s order this place’s recommended local sake.

539
00:29:53,613 --> 00:29:55,646
Yay! I’m excited!

540
00:29:55,669 --> 00:29:59,069
Let’s drink it together from little cups.

541
00:29:59,092 --> 00:30:00,930
Sounds good!

542
00:30:00,954 --> 00:30:04,687
I’ll have some sake too.

543
00:30:04,710 --> 00:30:08,244
I’ll call the server and place our order.

544
00:30:08,267 --> 00:30:11,556
Oh, let me call them for you.

545
00:30:11,579 --> 00:30:13,594
Excuse me~!

546
00:30:13,618 --> 00:30:16,418
So reliable!

547
00:30:16,441 --> 00:30:17,974
Thank you.

548
00:30:17,997 --> 00:30:22,476
Just drink at your own pace, okay?

549
00:30:22,500 --> 00:30:23,700
Got it.

550
00:30:23,723 --> 00:30:26,372
I’ll make sure not to overdo it.

551
00:30:26,396 --> 00:30:29,762
It’s better to drink water along with it.

552
00:30:29,785 --> 00:30:31,472
Good idea.

553
00:30:31,496 --> 00:30:34,229
Let’s order some cold water too.

554
00:30:34,252 --> 00:30:39,019
Drinking water with alcohol keeps you from getting too tipsy.

555
00:30:39,042 --> 00:30:41,910
You’re so thoughtful!

556
00:30:41,934 --> 00:30:44,136
You’re really something else.

557
00:30:44,159 --> 00:30:48,559
We both want to enjoy this till the end, after all.

558
00:30:48,582 --> 00:30:50,052
Got it.

559
00:30:50,075 --> 00:30:54,146
Let’s savor this delicious sake slowly.

560
00:30:54,170 --> 00:30:58,103
Now, let’s wait for our sake to arrive.

561
00:30:58,126 --> 00:30:59,626
Scene 14: How to Respond When You Drop Chopsticks

562
00:30:59,626 --> 00:31:05,460
Oh no! Oops—clatter!

563
00:31:05,483 --> 00:31:07,449
Are you okay?

564
00:31:07,472 --> 00:31:10,289
Did you hurt yourself?

565
00:31:10,313 --> 00:31:12,679
I’m so sorry.

566
00:31:12,702 --> 00:31:16,969
My hand slipped, and I dropped my chopsticks.

567
00:31:16,992 --> 00:31:19,625
I’m just glad you’re not hurt.

568
00:31:19,648 --> 00:31:23,892
I’m sorry for making a mess on the floor.

569
00:31:23,916 --> 00:31:28,149
Oh, don’t worry about it—just leave it.

570
00:31:28,172 --> 00:31:31,006
I’ll pick it up for you.

571
00:31:31,030 --> 00:31:36,563
No, no, I’ll get it—just stay put.

572
00:31:36,586 --> 00:31:38,675
I’m so sorry.

573
00:31:38,698 --> 00:31:41,196
Sorry for the trouble.

574
00:31:41,220 --> 00:31:45,153
I’ll bring you a new pair of chopsticks.

575
00:31:45,176 --> 00:31:46,870
Thank you.

576
00:31:46,893 --> 00:31:49,103
That’s such a relief!

577
00:31:49,127 --> 00:31:54,096
Would you prefer wooden disposable chopsticks or plastic ones?

578
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:58,920
Wooden ones would be great—they’re less slippery.

579
00:31:58,943 --> 00:32:01,277
Certainly.

580
00:32:01,301 --> 00:32:04,556
I’ll bring you wooden chopsticks.

581
00:32:04,579 --> 00:32:08,746
I’m worried if any food splashed on my clothes...

582
00:32:08,769 --> 00:32:12,102
Is your clothing stained at all?

583
00:32:12,125 --> 00:32:15,658
Would you like to use a refreshing hot towel?

584
00:32:15,681 --> 00:32:18,615
My clothes are fine, thank you.

585
00:32:18,638 --> 00:32:21,371
May I have a hot towel, please?

586
00:32:21,394 --> 00:32:23,194
Got it.

587
00:32:23,217 --> 00:32:27,307
Certainly! I’ll bring you a fresh hot towel and new chopsticks right away.

588
00:32:27,331 --> 00:32:30,698
Thank you so much for your quick response!

589
00:32:30,721 --> 00:32:34,054
Thank you for waiting.

590
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:38,124
Here are your disposable chopsticks and hot towel.

591
00:32:38,147 --> 00:32:41,186
Thank you so much for everything.

592
00:32:41,210 --> 00:32:45,850
I’ve wiped the floor clean as well, so please don’t worry.

593
00:32:45,873 --> 00:32:50,916
Your kindness really warmed my heart.

594
00:32:50,940 --> 00:32:55,906
I’m sorry for causing a disturbance during your meal.

595
00:32:55,929 --> 00:33:01,063
No, it was my fault for dropping my chopsticks.

596
00:33:01,086 --> 00:33:05,864
Please enjoy your meal before it gets cold.

597
00:33:05,887 --> 00:33:07,499
Got it.

598
00:33:07,523 --> 00:33:10,956
Yes, I’ll be careful not to drop them again.

599
00:33:10,979 --> 00:33:14,412
Please take your time and enjoy your meal.

600
00:33:14,436 --> 00:33:15,936
Thank you!

601
00:33:15,959 --> 00:33:17,892
Let’s eat!

602
00:33:17,915 --> 00:33:20,250
Please enjoy at your leisure.

603
00:33:20,274 --> 00:33:21,774
Scene 15: Handling Customer Service Incidents

604
00:33:21,774 --> 00:33:25,830
Manager, do you have a moment?

605
00:33:25,853 --> 00:33:27,630
What’s going on?

606
00:33:27,653 --> 00:33:30,387
Did something happen?

607
00:33:30,410 --> 00:33:36,666
Yes, a guest at table 3 accidentally broke a glass.

608
00:33:36,689 --> 00:33:40,907
Oh no, is anyone injured?

609
00:33:40,930 --> 00:33:44,697
No, fortunately, no one was hurt.

610
00:33:44,720 --> 00:33:46,886
That’s a relief.

611
00:33:46,909 --> 00:33:49,983
What’s the situation?

612
00:33:50,006 --> 00:33:56,140
It was a glass of red wine, and it splashed onto the floor and a bit on their clothes.

613
00:33:56,163 --> 00:34:00,298
So their clothes got stained too.

614
00:34:00,321 --> 00:34:02,593
That’s not good.

615
00:34:02,617 --> 00:34:06,687
The guest looks really sorry about it.

616
00:34:06,710 --> 00:34:11,710
Let’s bring cleaning supplies and a damp towel right away.

617
00:34:11,733 --> 00:34:16,300
I’ve prepared a broom and dustpan.

618
00:34:16,323 --> 00:34:21,540
Alright, the scattered glass shards are dangerous.

619
00:34:21,564 --> 00:34:25,164
I’ll sweep up the broken pieces.

620
00:34:25,187 --> 00:34:30,154
I’ll check on the guest’s clothes and apologize.

621
00:34:30,177 --> 00:34:34,444
Should we cover the dry-cleaning costs?

622
00:34:34,467 --> 00:34:39,151
Let’s assess the situation and offer our business card if needed.

623
00:34:39,174 --> 00:34:40,941
Got it.

624
00:34:40,964 --> 00:34:43,862
We’ll handle this calmly.

625
00:34:43,885 --> 00:34:48,328
Please guide other guests to avoid stepping on the glass.

626
00:34:48,352 --> 00:34:53,152
Yes, I’ll let the guests at the next table know as well.

627
00:34:53,175 --> 00:34:55,988
You’re handling this perfectly.

628
00:34:56,011 --> 00:34:58,302
Let’s act quickly.

629
00:34:58,326 --> 00:35:02,260
What about offering a new drink?

630
00:35:02,283 --> 00:35:06,090
Let’s serve them a complimentary glass of the same wine.

631
00:35:06,114 --> 00:35:08,388
Certainly.

632
00:35:08,411 --> 00:35:10,744
I’ll prepare it right away.

633
00:35:10,767 --> 00:35:15,134
No one was hurt, but let’s show our sincerity.

634
00:35:15,157 --> 00:35:19,290
Yes, having you here really helped, Manager.

635
00:35:19,313 --> 00:35:23,932
It’s thanks to you reporting it right away.

636
00:35:23,956 --> 00:35:25,694
Thank you.

637
00:35:25,717 --> 00:35:28,284
Alright, let’s go.

638
00:35:28,307 --> 00:35:32,473
Alright, let's head to table 3.

639
00:35:32,496 --> 00:35:35,173
Watch your step.

640
00:35:35,197 --> 00:35:36,730
Got it.

641
00:35:36,753 --> 00:35:38,320
Thanks.

642
00:35:38,343 --> 00:35:39,843
Scene 16: Pre-Break Handover

643
00:35:39,843 --> 00:35:45,939
The rush is over—it's quiet now.

644
00:35:45,962 --> 00:35:49,296
That was a crazy two hours, huh?

645
00:35:49,319 --> 00:35:54,588
I'm taking my 45-minute break now.

646
00:35:54,611 --> 00:35:56,814
Good work today!

647
00:35:56,837 --> 00:35:59,371
Make sure you rest up.

648
00:35:59,394 --> 00:36:04,194
Before I go, let me hand over a few things.

649
00:36:04,217 --> 00:36:05,617
Got it.

650
00:36:05,640 --> 00:36:07,848
I'll jot it down in the notebook.

651
00:36:07,872 --> 00:36:09,479
Please do.

652
00:36:09,503 --> 00:36:14,669
First, the customers at table 2 are waiting for dessert.

653
00:36:14,692 --> 00:36:20,492
What did they order? Two vanilla ice creams.

654
00:36:20,516 --> 00:36:22,716
Serve them in five minutes.

655
00:36:22,739 --> 00:36:24,506
Got it.

656
00:36:24,529 --> 00:36:27,529
Vanilla ice cream in five minutes—got it.

657
00:36:27,552 --> 00:36:32,952
Also, table 7’s bill is separate checks.

658
00:36:32,975 --> 00:36:35,608
Split payment calculations, right?

659
00:36:35,631 --> 00:36:38,110
I’ll handle it at the register.

660
00:36:38,133 --> 00:36:42,300
There’s a note on the receipt—check it.

661
00:36:42,323 --> 00:36:44,368
Understood.

662
00:36:44,392 --> 00:36:47,025
I’ll make sure there are no mistakes.

663
00:36:47,048 --> 00:36:51,181
Last orders in the kitchen are at 10:30.

664
00:36:51,204 --> 00:36:54,173
That’s in 30 minutes.

665
00:36:54,196 --> 00:36:57,455
Should I remind the customers?

666
00:36:57,478 --> 00:37:02,965
Please announce it to all tables 15 minutes before.

667
00:37:02,989 --> 00:37:06,789
Last order confirmation at 10:15—got it.

668
00:37:06,812 --> 00:37:08,145
Got it.

669
00:37:08,168 --> 00:37:10,301
I’m ready—let’s do this!

670
00:37:10,324 --> 00:37:13,821
Are the drinks on the floor restocked?

671
00:37:13,845 --> 00:37:18,578
I replaced the beer keg with a new one.

672
00:37:18,601 --> 00:37:21,010
As expected of you, senior.

673
00:37:21,034 --> 00:37:22,800
Perfect.

674
00:37:22,823 --> 00:37:24,390
Thank you.

675
00:37:24,413 --> 00:37:29,780
If anything goes wrong, knock on the break room door.

676
00:37:29,803 --> 00:37:31,662
Don't worry, I'm fine.

677
00:37:31,685 --> 00:37:34,454
I’ll hold down the fort solo!

678
00:37:34,478 --> 00:37:36,711
So reliable!

679
00:37:36,734 --> 00:37:39,380
I’m off to eat my staff meal.

680
00:37:39,404 --> 00:37:41,970
What’s today’s staff meal?

681
00:37:41,993 --> 00:37:46,193
The chef’s special extra-large curry rice!

682
00:37:46,216 --> 00:37:48,829
Wow, sounds great!

683
00:37:48,853 --> 00:37:51,228
Enjoy it!

684
00:37:51,251 --> 00:37:55,017
Hehe, I’ll save you a portion.

685
00:37:55,040 --> 00:37:58,574
Yes! Have a good break!

686
00:37:58,597 --> 00:38:00,097
Scene 17: Overeating and Leftovers

687
00:38:00,097 --> 00:38:04,330
Phew, I’m getting full.

688
00:38:04,353 --> 00:38:08,720
I’m stuffed too.

689
00:38:08,743 --> 00:38:13,958
But there’s still food left on the table.

690
00:38:13,981 --> 00:38:18,548
We ordered way too much at first.

691
00:38:18,572 --> 00:38:22,105
There are still three pieces of karaage left.

692
00:38:22,128 --> 00:38:26,895
These fried chicken pieces are huge, aren’t they?

693
00:38:26,918 --> 00:38:30,884
Can you eat a little more?

694
00:38:30,907 --> 00:38:36,197
I’m pretty full too, honestly.

695
00:38:36,221 --> 00:38:38,587
Please, just a bit more?

696
00:38:38,610 --> 00:38:41,589
Could you eat two more pieces?

697
00:38:41,613 --> 00:38:48,782
Hmm, it looks delicious, but I'm not sure if I can finish it. It'd be a waste to leave it, though.

698
00:38:48,805 --> 00:38:53,051
You're right, it's not good to waste food.

699
00:38:53,075 --> 00:38:58,694
You're a guy, so you should still have room in your stomach.

700
00:38:58,717 --> 00:39:00,559
Got it.

701
00:39:00,583 --> 00:39:03,762
I'll do my best to eat at least one.

702
00:39:03,785 --> 00:39:07,857
Don't just eat one—go for two!

703
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:11,897
Alright, let's squeeze some lemon on it to make it lighter.

704
00:39:11,921 --> 00:39:13,854
Good idea.

705
00:39:13,877 --> 00:39:17,337
Lemon makes it easier to eat.

706
00:39:17,360 --> 00:39:19,219
Okay, I ate one.

707
00:39:19,242 --> 00:39:22,132
It's crispy and so good!

708
00:39:22,156 --> 00:39:23,650
Wow.

709
00:39:23,673 --> 00:39:27,307
Alright, I'll power through the last one too.

710
00:39:27,330 --> 00:39:30,977
Oh, you don’t have to force yourself.

711
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:33,833
I won’t let you be the only one pushing yourself.

712
00:39:33,856 --> 00:39:35,990
I’ll eat too.

713
00:39:36,013 --> 00:39:39,246
Heh, you don’t want to lose, huh?

714
00:39:39,269 --> 00:39:41,343
Let’s eat!

715
00:39:41,367 --> 00:39:45,204
Ugh, it’s tough, but it’s so good.

716
00:39:45,227 --> 00:39:48,560
I finished another one too.

717
00:39:48,583 --> 00:39:51,067
We did it!

718
00:39:51,090 --> 00:39:53,724
The plate’s all clean now.

719
00:39:53,748 --> 00:39:56,415
Mission accomplished—we finished it all!

720
00:39:56,438 --> 00:39:59,004
Feels great, doesn’t it?

721
00:39:59,027 --> 00:40:04,227
Next time, let’s think about portion sizes when we order.

722
00:40:04,250 --> 00:40:05,787
Good idea.

723
00:40:05,811 --> 00:40:08,984
Getting too greedy is dangerous.

724
00:40:09,007 --> 00:40:12,774
But I’m glad we didn’t leave anything.

725
00:40:12,797 --> 00:40:17,363
I feel like my stomach’s about to burst—let’s take a break.

726
00:40:17,386 --> 00:40:18,886
Scene 18: The Last Train / Rushing for the Last Train

727
00:40:18,886 --> 00:40:21,624
What time is it?

728
00:40:21,648 --> 00:40:24,881
Do you have the time?

729
00:40:24,904 --> 00:40:30,238
Uh, it’s exactly 11:15.

730
00:40:30,261 --> 00:40:34,599
What?! Already?!

731
00:40:34,622 --> 00:40:39,640
Time really flies, doesn’t it?

732
00:40:39,664 --> 00:40:43,997
When’s your last train?

733
00:40:44,020 --> 00:40:48,987
Mine’s at 11:45.

734
00:40:49,010 --> 00:40:53,693
My last train is at 11:30!

735
00:40:53,716 --> 00:40:57,089
Only 15 minutes left!

736
00:40:57,112 --> 00:40:59,746
That’s cutting it close!

737
00:40:59,769 --> 00:41:02,583
We’ve gotta leave now or we’ll miss it!

738
00:41:02,606 --> 00:41:06,540
It takes about 10 minutes to walk to the station, right?

739
00:41:06,563 --> 00:41:10,940
We could make it in 5 if we run, but it’d be risky.

740
00:41:10,963 --> 00:41:15,196
We’ll definitely be late if we don’t leave now.

741
00:41:15,219 --> 00:41:17,839
Let’s hurry with the bill.

742
00:41:17,862 --> 00:41:20,359
I’ll call the server.

743
00:41:20,382 --> 00:41:23,751
Okay, I’ll get my wallet ready.

744
00:41:23,775 --> 00:41:27,908
I’ll cover the bill—you go ahead.

745
00:41:27,931 --> 00:41:31,774
Oh, you don’t have to do that!

746
00:41:31,797 --> 00:41:35,174
Just pay me back later on LINE.

747
00:41:35,198 --> 00:41:36,888
Really?

748
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:39,598
I’m so sorry about this.

749
00:41:39,621 --> 00:41:41,221
You’re a lifesaver!

750
00:41:41,244 --> 00:41:44,778
Here, grab your coat and bag!

751
00:41:44,801 --> 00:41:47,267
Make sure you haven't forgotten anything.

752
00:41:47,290 --> 00:41:49,324
I've got my umbrella too.

753
00:41:49,347 --> 00:41:53,780
Don’t run—just walk briskly to the station, okay?

754
00:41:53,803 --> 00:41:54,936
Got it!

755
00:41:54,959 --> 00:41:58,736
I had such a great time today.

756
00:41:58,759 --> 00:42:00,537
Thank you!

757
00:42:00,561 --> 00:42:03,427
I had a great time too.

758
00:42:03,450 --> 00:42:06,017
Let me know when you get home.

759
00:42:06,040 --> 00:42:08,286
Got it.

760
00:42:08,309 --> 00:42:11,676
I’ll text you once I’m safely on the train.

761
00:42:11,699 --> 00:42:14,432
Have a safe trip home!

762
00:42:14,455 --> 00:42:17,267
Check, please!

763
00:42:17,291 --> 00:42:19,691
That was delicious!

764
00:42:19,714 --> 00:42:23,209
Sure thing! Leave it to me.

765
00:42:23,232 --> 00:42:25,166
Run!

766
00:42:25,189 --> 00:42:26,649
Got it!

767
00:42:26,672 --> 00:42:28,808
Goodnight!

768
00:42:28,832 --> 00:42:30,876
Goodnight!

769
00:42:30,899 --> 00:42:32,956
Hurry up!

770
00:42:32,979 --> 00:42:36,513
Oh, and be careful on your way home.

771
00:42:36,536 --> 00:42:38,987
Yes, thank you!

772
00:42:39,010 --> 00:42:42,983
Phew, I hope we make it in time.

773
00:42:43,007 --> 00:42:44,507
Scene 19: Finishing Up Dinner – Off to Karaoke!

774
00:42:44,507 --> 00:42:47,440
We’ve left the restaurant.

775
00:42:47,463 --> 00:42:50,430
The breeze feels nice.

776
00:42:50,453 --> 00:42:52,820
That was so good, wasn’t it?

777
00:42:52,843 --> 00:42:56,293
I’m stuffed.

778
00:42:56,316 --> 00:42:59,849
It’s still before 10 o’clock.

779
00:42:59,872 --> 00:43:02,125
That was fast!

780
00:43:02,149 --> 00:43:04,749
It really does!

781
00:43:04,772 --> 00:43:08,138
What should we do next?

782
00:43:08,161 --> 00:43:12,361
Should we hit up another place?

783
00:43:12,384 --> 00:43:14,828
After-party, huh?

784
00:43:14,851 --> 00:43:17,651
How about karaoke?

785
00:43:17,674 --> 00:43:19,968
Karaoke.

786
00:43:19,992 --> 00:43:21,926
Sounds good!

787
00:43:21,950 --> 00:43:24,517
I wanna sing!

788
00:43:24,540 --> 00:43:29,583
I haven’t sung in ages—I wanna belt out a bunch of songs!

789
00:43:29,606 --> 00:43:34,206
A quiet bar where we can relax and chat sounds nice too.

790
00:43:34,229 --> 00:43:38,195
Bars have such a sophisticated vibe.

791
00:43:38,218 --> 00:43:40,852
What’s your mood?

792
00:43:40,875 --> 00:43:45,930
I’m feeling hyped today—karaoke it is!

793
00:43:45,954 --> 00:43:48,003
It’s settled!

794
00:43:48,026 --> 00:43:50,886
Let’s go to karaoke!

795
00:43:50,909 --> 00:43:54,343
There’s a great karaoke spot nearby.

796
00:43:54,366 --> 00:43:57,499
Is it close to the station?

797
00:43:57,522 --> 00:43:58,655
Got it.

798
00:43:58,678 --> 00:44:01,950
Just a three-minute walk.

799
00:44:01,974 --> 00:44:04,807
Should we go for the all-you-can-drink plan?

800
00:44:04,830 --> 00:44:07,397
Still up for more drinks?

801
00:44:07,420 --> 00:44:10,296
I’m good with just some oolong tea.

802
00:44:10,320 --> 00:44:13,653
Let’s sing and drink for just an hour.

803
00:44:13,676 --> 00:44:15,609
Sounds good to me.

804
00:44:15,632 --> 00:44:18,684
Let’s not stay out too late.

805
00:44:18,708 --> 00:44:22,280
We’ve got work tomorrow, after all.

806
00:44:22,304 --> 00:44:25,837
We *have* to be home before the last train.

807
00:44:25,860 --> 00:44:29,227
What’s the first song you’re gonna sing?

808
00:44:29,250 --> 00:44:33,883
Let's sing some nostalgic '90s pop hits!

809
00:44:33,906 --> 00:44:35,673
Great choice!

810
00:44:35,696 --> 00:44:38,963
I'll sing along with you.

811
00:44:38,987 --> 00:44:42,320
How about we sing a duet too?

812
00:44:42,343 --> 00:44:44,010
Sounds fun!

813
00:44:44,033 --> 00:44:46,284
Let's make it a blast!

814
00:44:46,307 --> 00:44:50,473
Alright, let's head to the karaoke bar!

815
00:44:50,496 --> 00:44:52,063
Got it.

816
00:44:52,086 --> 00:44:54,219
Please lead the way.

817
00:44:54,242 --> 00:44:56,376
Right this way, please.

818
00:44:56,399 --> 00:44:58,332
Follow me.

819
00:44:58,355 --> 00:44:59,855
Scene 20: Basics of Payment

820
00:44:59,855 --> 00:45:01,855
Welcome!

821
00:45:01,878 --> 00:45:04,170
We're ready to pay.

822
00:45:04,193 --> 00:45:05,593
Got it.

823
00:45:05,616 --> 00:45:08,657
Here's the bill.

824
00:45:08,680 --> 00:45:10,151
Please do.

825
00:45:10,175 --> 00:45:11,869
Thank you.

826
00:45:11,893 --> 00:45:15,064
I'll take the bill.

827
00:45:15,087 --> 00:45:18,421
How much is the total for today?

828
00:45:18,444 --> 00:45:22,578
The total comes to 8,500 yen.

829
00:45:22,601 --> 00:45:24,368
Got it.

830
00:45:24,391 --> 00:45:27,724
Can I use a credit card?

831
00:45:27,747 --> 00:45:29,314
Got it.

832
00:45:29,337 --> 00:45:33,024
We accept all major credit cards.

833
00:45:33,048 --> 00:45:35,427
I'll pay with my Visa card.

834
00:45:35,451 --> 00:45:38,084
Certainly.

835
00:45:38,107 --> 00:45:40,840
I'll take your card.

836
00:45:40,863 --> 00:45:43,537
I'd like to pay in full.

837
00:45:43,560 --> 00:45:45,960
One-time payment, correct?

838
00:45:45,983 --> 00:45:49,670
Please tap your card here.

839
00:45:49,694 --> 00:45:51,591
Beep...

840
00:45:51,614 --> 00:45:53,548
Is that it?

841
00:45:53,571 --> 00:45:55,304
Got it.

842
00:45:55,327 --> 00:45:58,094
Your contactless payment is complete.

843
00:45:58,117 --> 00:46:02,117
Modern registers are so convenient!

844
00:46:02,140 --> 00:46:06,173
It's so handy to pay quickly like this.

845
00:46:06,196 --> 00:46:10,163
May I have the receipt and an official receipt?

846
00:46:10,186 --> 00:46:11,719
Got it.

847
00:46:11,742 --> 00:46:15,009
I'll issue both for you.

848
00:46:15,032 --> 00:46:19,087
Please make the official receipt out to 'To Whom It May Concern.'

849
00:46:19,110 --> 00:46:21,193
Certainly.

850
00:46:21,217 --> 00:46:24,017
I'll make it out to 'To Whom It May Concern.'

851
00:46:24,040 --> 00:46:27,840
Could we have paid separately?

852
00:46:27,863 --> 00:46:29,596
Got it.

853
00:46:29,619 --> 00:46:32,953
Yes, we can handle separate checks.

854
00:46:32,976 --> 00:46:36,746
Next time, I'll split the bill with friends.

855
00:46:36,769 --> 00:46:39,418
Please feel free to use that option.

856
00:46:39,442 --> 00:46:42,808
The food was really delicious.

857
00:46:42,831 --> 00:46:45,231
Thank you for the meal.

858
00:46:45,254 --> 00:46:46,821
Thank you.

859
00:46:46,844 --> 00:46:49,525
We're so glad to hear that!

860
00:46:49,549 --> 00:46:51,582
We'll come again.

861
00:46:51,605 --> 00:46:56,338
Here's your receipt, official receipt, and card.

862
00:46:56,361 --> 00:46:57,828
Got it.

863
00:46:57,851 --> 00:47:00,053
I've received them.

864
00:47:00,077 --> 00:47:03,277
Thank you for visiting today.

865
00:47:03,300 --> 00:47:05,598
We hope to see you again.

866
00:47:05,622 --> 00:47:07,155
Thank you very much.

867
00:47:07,178 --> 00:47:09,453
Goodbye.